## Summary

An interrupted first `open --item` cannot recover if an unrelated native edit changes the target item's `updated_at` before retry. The retry creates a different CAS plan but reuses the original transaction ID, so the SDK refuses the journal-plan mismatch on every subsequent attempt.

Reproduced on PR #1 at `a7ff9519c4b7155859d331a9f79fd6b41749dafb`, package version `2026.10.25`, Node `24.22.1`, and the pinned `@unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.24`, using a fresh synthetic filesystem tracker.

## Minimal SDK reproduction

Save as `repro.ts` at that checkout's root and run `node repro.ts` with its dependencies available:

```ts
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { mkdtemp, rm } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import { PmClient, WorkspaceTransactionInterruptedError } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk';
import { open, matrix } from './index.ts';

const root = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'hypothesis-open-retry-'));
try {
  const workspace = join(root, '.agents', 'pm');
  const client = new PmClient({ pmRoot: workspace, author: 'fixture', noExtensions: true });
  await client.init('hyp', { defaults: true, agentGuidance: 'skip', mergeFence: false });
  await client.create({
    id: 'hyp-owner', type: 'Issue', title: 'Synthetic owner', createMode: 'progressive',
  });
  const options = { workspace, author: 'fixture', item: 'hyp-owner' };
  await assert.rejects(open('Attached investigation', {
    ...options,
    onTransition(event) {
      if (event.transition === 'prepared' && event.transactionId.includes('-owner-'))
        throw new WorkspaceTransactionInterruptedError();
    },
  }), WorkspaceTransactionInterruptedError);
  await client.update('hyp-owner', {
    title: 'Unrelated changed title', message: 'Synthetic independent edit',
  });
  await open('Attached investigation', options);
  assert.equal((await matrix('hyp-owner', options)).revision, 0);
} finally {
  await rm(root, { recursive: true, force: true });
}
```

Expected: re-read the current native item and initialize the still-absent investigation state with a fresh plan matching its current `updated_at`. Preserve the unrelated title edit.

Actual: public `open` throws `HypothesisError` with code `sdk` and a remedy advising the caller to retry the same operation. Repeating that operation continues to fail. Inspecting the underlying package operation produced `PmCliError: Workspace transaction … journal does not match the supplied plan` on two consecutive retries.

## Cause and contract

[`Store.commit`](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-hypothesis/blob/a7ff9519c4b7155859d331a9f79fd6b41749dafb/src/store.ts#L80-L85) uses `updated_at` as the initialization precondition when `hypothesis_state` is absent. But its transaction ID hashes only the item ID, absent `hypothesis_state`, and desired envelope, omitting the actual `updated_at` precondition. Therefore the changed plan collides with the interrupted journal.

[`open`](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-hypothesis/blob/a7ff9519c4b7155859d331a9f79fd6b41749dafb/src/hypothesis.ts#L9-L19) delegates initialization directly to that commit path. The [documented recovery contract](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-hypothesis/blob/a7ff9519c4b7155859d331a9f79fd6b41749dafb/ARCHITECTURE.md#L29-L35) says transaction IDs include the current precondition and that interrupted, unapplied intents whose preconditions changed obtain a fresh plan. The package also describes open as having deterministic replay identity.

This is not a request to bypass the stale-plan guard: that guard correctly prevents replay of a mismatched plan. The package needs to give a newly computed initialization plan its own identity.

## Acceptance

- Include the actual initialization match key/value in owner transaction identity.
- Cover interruption at the initial owner's `prepared` boundary, an unrelated native edit, and rerunning the same `open`.
- The retry initializes exactly once, preserves the unrelated edit, and subsequent retries are no-ops.
- A genuinely initialized or incompatible current owner must still be revalidated rather than overwritten.
- Do not require raw journal deletion or replay to recover.

Canonical owner: [pm-hypothesis PR #1](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-hypothesis/pull/1), specifically its transaction identity construction. Existing observation/withdrawal/conclusion recovery tests passed; this finding is scoped to initialization and does not claim lost data or a broken SDK guard.



